Done and committed. 🐙

What changed (src/agent_builder.rs, +docs line in `CLAUDE.md`):

• `model_identity_note(provider, model)` — a facts-only block: names the provider and model id, states that pair is the only evidence about which model it is, that it has no direct knowledge of its architecture/training/vendor, and that anything it feels certain about there is a training prior — report the pair and nothing more. It also names the front-end label (the tool running it) as non-evidence, which is the same reasoning the DeepSeek model correctly applied to "yoyo" before asserting "Claude" on exactly as little.
• **`compose_system_prompt(base, provider, model)`** — appends the note after the resolved prompt; empty/whitespace base yields just the note (no leading blank lines).
• Call sites in the same edit (the #618/#647/#653/#658 revert shape): configure_agent's single with_system_prompt — which runs after `resolve_system_prompt, so it covers default / --system / --system-file / config — plus build_side_agent`, since "who are you" is exactly the kind of thing asked in a one-shot /side. Architect/editor builders untouched to keep the diff one file, small.

Tests (5, all in agent_builder.rs): provider+model appear in the note; `("deepseek","deepseek-v4-flash") contains neither Anthropic nor Claude; no yoyo` persona (identity stays in the protected files a product user doesn't have); `"You are Jarvis."` still starts the composed prompt; empty base composes to the bare note.

Verified: cargo fmt --check clean, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean, full suite 4634 + 89 passing, 0 failed.

One honest limitation I did not fix: this makes the model report the provider/model id truthfully, but yoyo can't verify the id either — an OpenAI-compatible endpoint can serve whatever it likes under any model string. The note says the pair is the only evidence available, not that the pair is true.
